# id: M70-ingest-does-not-seed-the-clock
# covering-test: TestARangeIngestingRecordsRaisesItsClock
# package: ./store/
# expect: killed
# power-seeds: 1
# power-floor: 1
# power-ceiling: 1
# power-measured: killed deterministically by its covering test. Two corrections were needed first, both mine: the test's timestamps were below the simulated clock so the floor never bound, and then five seconds ahead so Update refused them as beyond maxOffset. A hundred milliseconds is the realistic gap and the one that must work
# mutates: BUG-023's second half. Records arriving by any path -- a split's birth state, an installed snapshot, a restart's recovery -- no longer raise the range's clock to the maximum timestamp among them. A range built from a SNAPSHOT rather than by applying the split entry gets no floor at all, which is the half a fix that only touched the split path would miss
